# Ethernaut Level 2 — Fallout

**Vulnerability:** Typo in constructor name
**Category:** Access Control
**Severity:** Critical
**Real-world example:** Rubixi protocol hack (2016)

## Attack Path
1. Call Fal1out() — the misnamed "constructor"
2. owner = attacker
3. collectAllocations() — drain contract

## Root Cause
Solidity 0.6.x constructors required exact name match with contract.
Fal1out ≠ Fallout — one character typo made it a public function.
Owner was never initialized (address(0)) until attacker called it.

## Fix
Use the constructor keyword (Solidity 0.7.0+).
Never rely on function-name-based constructors.
